From e2f46e0e2c5e792f601c03d807dc25ef513b8b43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pugant <pugant@localhost>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 09:14:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] common: keep tool-call arg streaming append-only on
 duplicate leniency
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The 04/09 last-wins leniency erased the earlier pair and re-emitted it at
the end, REORDERING the accumulated args string mid-stream. The streaming
diff (string_diff, called from common_chat_msg_diff::compute_diffs)
requires each partial parse to extend the previous one, so every leniency
turn died client-side with "Invalid diff: '<args>' not found at start of
'<reordered args>'" — the leniency converted a grammar death into a
stream death and saved nothing end-to-end (pi_agent errata 05/09 09:06;
verified server-side: 7/7 cancel events map 1:1 to the 7 grammar
deviations, each <=0.5 ms after its marker, zero other cancels in 782
requests).

Duplicates now simply APPEND (duplicate JSON key); last-wins is resolved
at parse time by any standard JSON parser, which is also what the
server-side completeness check sees. The mapper becomes append-only by
construction and the arg_pair_pos offset bookkeeping collapses into a
seen-name set used only for the leniency-hit marker.

Test: duplicate_streaming_append_only drives the production streaming
path (common_chat_parse partial + compute_diffs) over the 04/09 shape
(path, content, path) — failed exactly at the duplicate step before the
fix. 04/09 duplicate test stays green (marker + last-wins semantics).
Suites green: test-chat-auto-parser 79/609, test-chat-peg-parser 32/198.
NOT deployed: prepared only, joint test live on optim3.

Co-Authored-By: GLM by z.ai <noreply@z.ai>
